# Provider (Azure/GCP) credential encryption-at-rest key -- app/credentials.py
# auto-generates this file on first use if CREDENTIAL_ENCRYPTION_KEY isn't set
# in the environment. It decrypts every Azure client secret / GCP service-
# account key stored in provider_credentials -- committing it would defeat
# that encryption entirely, the same class of incident fix_p0_credential_leak.py
# already had to clean up once for session cookies/passwords. Never commit.
config/credential.key
*.patch

# --- added by audit r01: guard the CLASSES of leak that actually happened ---
# db/backups/ alone was added only AFTER two mysqldump files (admin/viewer/editor
# password hashes, account ids, audit rows) had already been committed; a dump
# written anywhere else would still have been picked up by `git add .`.
# Env variants (staging/local/dev ...) -- the two committed templates stay tracked.
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.production.example
